{"name":"Chronicle","hex":"#3e4265","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chronicle","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A written account of events and when they happened, ordered by time."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To record in or as in a chronicle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chronicle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chronicle","blocks":[{"text":"A chronicle is a historical account of events arranged in chronological order, as in a timeline. Typically, equal weight is given for historically important events and local events, the purpose being the recording of events that occurred, seen from the perspective of the chronicler. A chronicle which traces world history is a universal chronicle. This is in contrast to a narrative or history, in which an author chooses events to interpret and analyze and excludes those the author does not consider important or relevant."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/K%C3%A9pes_kr%C3%B3nika_-_1.oldal_-_Nagy_Lajos_kir%C3%A1ly_a_tr%C3%B3non%2C_Szent_Katalin%2C_Krisztus_%C3%A9s_a_magyar_uralkod%C3%B3i_c%C3%ADmerek.jpg/330px-K%C3%A9pes_kr%C3%B3nika_-_1.oldal_-_Nagy_Lajos_kir%C3%A1ly_a_tr%C3%B3non%2C_Szent_Katalin%2C_Krisztus_%C3%A9s_a_magyar_uralkod%C3%B3i_c%C3%ADmerek.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chronicle"},{"title":"Chronicle (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Chronicle is a 2012 American film directed by Josh Trank in his feature-length directorial debut, and written by Max Landis. It follows three Seattle high school seniors—bullied Andrew, his cousin Matt, and the popular Steve —who form a bond after gaining telekinetic powers from an unknown object and using them for fun, until Andrew begins going down a darker path."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f9/Chronicle_Film_Poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled",